  "@type": "Process",
  "critical": false,
  "description": "Design pedagogy for digital-to-analog converters (DACs): the R-2R ladder as the dominant binary-weighted resistor network, weighted-resistor (string) architectures, PWM-filtered DACs, and the static/dynamic specifications (resolution, monotonicity, settling time, glitch energy) that govern accuracy and speed. Teaches how to reconstruct an analog voltage from a digital word, building on analog switches from semiconductor-devices and precision matched resistors from passive-components.",
